[{"client_msg_id":"b09c70df-7428-49f9-b561-3f0e730b0bad","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"メソッド記法をどれくらい積極的に使っていくべきか未だに悩んでいる","ts":"1624885061.257400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"WOSr"}]},{"client_msg_id":"e3fcb95a-e02d-4509-8789-9ba3b4fc5bb1","type":"message","user":"U7H4TJEG0","text":"issueにも書いてますが、衝突するのは `:` (辞書 vs 変数名) と `#` (コメント vs autload) くらいだと思います (他に知っている人はコメントしておいてください)。","ts":"1624856624.256400","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"naruhodo","count":2,"users":["UL6CFN8NR","U7JL1UKKL"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"74kxO"}]},{"client_msg_id":"9bb75952-7e21-4fb9-98b4-3db1fb08a0c6","type":"message","user":"UL6CFN8NR","text":"これってスペースを省略可能にすることで新たに問題が生じたりするんでしょうか？たとえば、他の文法とコンフリクトするとか。\n\nよくあるのは論理積 \u0026amp;\u0026amp; とビット積 \u0026amp; と参照演算子 \u0026amp; のコンフリクトとかですね","ts":"1624856457.254400","edited":{"user":"UL6CFN8NR","ts":"1624856484.000000"},"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"e8E"}]},{"client_msg_id":"27992dab-cbae-4d35-a8e4-5e22be69c592","type":"message","user":"U7H4TJEG0","text":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim/issues/7338\u003e こちらReopenしたので議論を進めたい人はコメントお願いします。","ts":"1624855405.252000","attachments":[{"color":"36a64f","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim/issues/7338|#7338 Vim9: strict white space check is not developer friendly\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim/issues/7338|#7338 Vim9: strict white space check is not developer friendly\u003e","text":"*Problems*\n\nCurrently (v8.2.2029), Vim9 checks white spaces strictly. It enforces white  \nspace everywhere; around binary operators, assignment operators, function  \narguments, dictionary keys and comment symbol. However, this smells like an  \nancient language and is frustration for me. Most modern languages have lexers  \nand skips white spaces while scanning the source code (indentations are  \nexception; I couldn't find a language confiders spaces between tokens, maybe  \nTeX is one of them, but legacy language anyway). Enforcing white spaces is  \nnot developer friendly and cannot be considered as a modern language IMO.\n\nSome languages have linters or formatters which defines the number of white  \nspaces, but in language specification, white spaces are optional between tokens.  \nSome language formatters prefers omitting spaces due to precedence; `a*b + c*d`.  \nSome people like spaces all the way, and others don't. Formatters often suggest  \nthe standard style for that language, but they _fix_ valid code to valid code.\n\n*Specification changes suggestion*\n\n• Allow omitting white spaces around binary operators (`+`, `-`, `..`, `*`, `/`,  \n    `%`, `==`, `==#`, `\u0026gt;`, `=~`, etc) and assignment operators (`=`, `+=`, `..=`,  \n    `=\u0026lt;\u0026lt;` etc).\n• Allow omitting white spaces after commas in function arguments (both `:def`  \n    and `:call`), arrays and dictionaries.\n• Keep enforcing spaces after `:` in dictionaries and around `#` for comments.\n    • `:` conflicts with scopes and `#` conflicts with autoload function names.","fields":[{"title":"Labels","value":"enhancement","short":true},{"title":"Comments","value":"3","short":true}],"mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim|vim/vim\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png","ts":1605971044}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"T51"}]},{"client_msg_id":"4925537c-413b-4b2a-b215-2e552ca4affa","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"人力だとあまり恩恵なさそう","ts":"1624855274.251400","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"sorena","count":3,"users":["U776661HA","UL6CFN8NR","U9S4G0LJW"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"qII/"}]},{"client_msg_id":"d6a2e9b4-d157-4f92-a211-81d4afb0912e","type":"message","user":"U7JL1UKKL","text":"go fmtみたいなのを強制したかったとか？","ts":"1624854615.251100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"KqDs"}]},{"client_msg_id":"ab826b5b-80cf-4bdd-9411-1028e3ece56c","type":"message","user":"U7H4TJEG0","text":"スターは4つ付いたけどコメントは1人しかいなかったのであまり関心が持たれなかったようだし個人的なモチベも下がった…","ts":"1624850608.250200","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"totemoturai","count":2,"users":["U776661HA","U7JL1UKKL"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"gHDS"}]},{"client_msg_id":"147d82d6-efe9-4ffe-ba7c-ef7c2542fff3","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"それ…","ts":"1624850468.248800","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"oP1lx"}]},{"client_msg_id":"cd26167f-3afe-4afe-82ff-f7f1cfeb4cee","type":"message","user":"U7H4TJEG0","text":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim/issues/7338\u003e こういう話ですかね？援護・賛同してくれる人があまりいなかったので閉じました。","ts":"1624850431.248500","attachments":[{"color":"cb2431","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim/issues/7338|#7338 Vim9: strict white space check is not developer friendly\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim/issues/7338|#7338 Vim9: strict white space check is not developer friendly\u003e","text":"*Problems*\n\nCurrently (v8.2.2029), Vim9 checks white spaces strictly. It enforces white  \nspace everywhere; around binary operators, assignment operators, function  \narguments, dictionary keys and comment symbol. However, this smells like an  \nancient language and is frustration for me. Most modern languages have lexers  \nand skips white spaces while scanning the source code (indentations are  \nexception; I couldn't find a language confiders spaces between tokens, maybe  \nTeX is one of them, but legacy language anyway). Enforcing white spaces is  \nnot developer friendly and cannot be considered as a modern language IMO.\n\nSome languages have linters or formatters which defines the number of white  \nspaces, but in language specification, white spaces are optional between tokens.  \nSome language formatters prefers omitting spaces due to precedence; `a*b + c*d`.  \nSome people like spaces all the way, and others don't. Formatters often suggest  \nthe standard style for that language, but they _fix_ valid code to valid code.\n\n*Specification changes suggestion*\n\n• Allow omitting white spaces around binary operators (`+`, `-`, `..`, `*`, `/`,  \n    `%`, `==`, `==#`, `\u0026gt;`, `=~`, etc) and assignment operators (`=`, `+=`, `..=`,  \n    `=\u0026lt;\u0026lt;` etc).\n• Allow omitting white spaces after commas in function arguments (both `:def`  \n    and `:call`), arrays and dictionaries.\n• Keep enforcing spaces after `:` in dictionaries and around `#` for comments.\n    • `:` conflicts with scopes and `#` conflicts with autoload function names.","fields":[{"title":"Labels","value":"enhancement","short":true},{"title":"Comments","value":"3","short":true}],"mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim/vim|vim/vim\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png","ts":1605971044}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"MvdW/"}]},{"client_msg_id":"fc29d0a0-2f8a-48ba-b7c7-0eea06a9b903","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"スペース必須な箇所ありますね","ts":"1624850233.246300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"eTd"}]},{"client_msg_id":"5e7ae716-92a0-4830-936d-df94e1ef7f5d","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"今はどうなってるんだろう","ts":"1624850216.245600","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"T0k92"}]},{"client_msg_id":"e5f7019c-07eb-4a29-8fc1-a0e0f64cc7f8","type":"messa